  <ConferenceTracks
    title="Exciting Tracks and Workshops"
    day1Title="Day 1 — May 5"
    day1Subtitle="Conference, Workshops, Training & Hackathon"
    day2Title="Day 2 — May 6"
    day2Subtitle="Conference & Hackathon Finals"
    day1Tracks={[
      {
        title: "Agentic AI Summit",
        text: "2026 marks a pivotal year for the explosive growth of the agentic ecosystem. This summit focuses on the core standards and evolving software paradigms of agentic systems, exploring protocols like MCP and A2A, as well as emerging trends in sovereign AI. We will dissect new AI software development models driven by tools like Codex. Bringing together innovative startups, creators, venture capitalists, and enterprise leaders, this event is dedicated to charting the innovative pathways and commercial future of open-source agents.",
      },
      {
        title: "Open Source Robotics",
        text: "While large models give robots a \"soul,\" open source is forging their \"body.\" This track showcases the latest advancements and innovations in open-source platforms and applications for Embodied AI. Through a dynamic mix of keynote speeches and hands-on workshops, you will learn to build autonomous robotics systems and real-world AI applications using open-source frameworks. This is the ultimate proving ground where hardware meets algorithms to define the next generation of embodied intelligence.",
        link: "/open-source-robotics",
      },
      {
        title: "Agentic App",
        text: "From intent-driven AI-native applications to the \"Internet of Agents,\" this track covers the full stack of the agentic era. Explore multimodal generation, creative workflows with frameworks like Makepad Splash and A2UI, alongside key protocols like MCP and ACP and open-source coding agents like OpenClaw and Claude Code. Whether you're building the next generative hit or co-creating infrastructure for multi-agent collaboration, this is where it all comes together.",
      },
      {
        title: "Agentic AI on Edge",
        text: "On-device AI is experiencing a performance awakening akin to Nano Banana 2, with agentic AI rapidly infiltrating edge devices. This forum focuses on deploying powerful AI models in resource-constrained environments, diving deep into engineering practices for on-device inference acceleration, model compression, and real-time decision-making. Join us to explore how AI can unleash ultimate local intelligence even in offline and low-power scenarios.",
      },
      {
        title: "AI Hardware",
        text: "In 2026, an era where \"computing power is national strength,\" every evolution in hardware architecture redefines the ceiling of massive models. Connecting the Paris and Shenzhen GOSIM communities, this track focuses on top-tier AI silicon, accelerator ecosystems, and hardware-software co-optimization, exploring how open-source hardware trends can break industry monopolies. This is the ultimate gathering for global silicon geeks and hardware founders building the most efficient computing engines for agentic systems.",
      },
    ]}
    day2Tracks={[
      {
        title: "Agentic AI Summit",
        text: "2026 marks a pivotal year for the explosive growth of the agentic ecosystem. This summit focuses on the core standards and evolving software paradigms of agentic systems, exploring protocols like MCP and A2A, as well as emerging trends in sovereign AI. We will dissect new AI software development models driven by tools like Codex. Bringing together innovative startups, creators, venture capitalists, and enterprise leaders, this event is dedicated to charting the innovative pathways and commercial future of open-source agents.",
      },
      {
        title: "Open Source Robotics",
        text: "While large models give robots a \"soul,\" open source is forging their \"body.\" This track showcases the latest advancements and innovations in open-source platforms and applications for Embodied AI. Through a dynamic mix of keynote speeches and hands-on workshops, you will learn to build autonomous robotics systems and real-world AI applications using open-source frameworks. This is the ultimate proving ground where hardware meets algorithms to define the next generation of embodied intelligence.",
        link: "/open-source-robotics",
      },
      {
        title: "Agentic App",
        text: "From intent-driven AI-native applications to the \"Internet of Agents,\" this track covers the full stack of the agentic era. Explore multimodal generation, creative workflows with frameworks like Makepad Splash and A2UI, alongside key protocols like MCP and ACP and open-source coding agents like OpenClaw and Claude Code. Whether you're building the next generative hit or co-creating infrastructure for multi-agent collaboration, this is where it all comes together.",
      },
      {
        title: "Open Source Model",
        text: "Open-source models are reaching a paradigm-shifting inflection point where \"small models punch above their weight.\" Covering open foundation models across LLMs, audio, image, and video, this track spotlights the latest technological evolutions and application breakthroughs. From general-purpose capabilities to domain-specific verticals, open-source models are relentlessly pushing the boundaries of what AI can achieve.",
      },
    ]}
    highlightsTitle="Spotlight & Hackathon"
    highlights={[
      {
        title: "GOSIM Spotlight 2026: Frontier Creators",
        text: "Say goodbye to pure slide decks and welcome the ultimate showdown in the era of \"AI Pragmatism\"! The GOSIM Spotlight Demo will handpick the world's most commercially promising open-source AI generative projects for hardcore, live on-stage demonstrations. Selected creators will not only receive full travel sponsorships to fly to Paris but will also pitch directly to global top-tier investors and tech visionaries, claiming their open-source spotlight moment.",
        link: "https://spotlight.gosim.org/paris2026/",
      },
      {
        title: "Robotics Hackathon",
        text: "A hands-on robotics hackathon featuring OpenArm — a fully open-source 7 DoF humanoid robot arm. Apply state-of-the-art models on physical hardware to solve challenges in robotic grasping and manipulation. Teams of 3–5 people, with remote access available.",
        link: "/unaite-hackathon",
      },
    ]}
  />

